steps.text:
That’s expected in this older Tailwind version: `border-dotted` only supplies the *style*, not a visible border width.

`@apply border-dotted;` effectively becomes:

```css
border-width: 0;
border-style: dotted;
```

So it remains invisible. Apply a border-width utility too:

```css
.foo {
  @apply border border-dotted;
}
```

(or `@apply border-2 border-dashed`, etc.)

`borderStylesReset` intentionally forces dotted/dashed alone not to create a border; the later `borderStyles` generator adds `border-style`. They don’t overwrite each other—they produce the two declarations above. If `.border-dotted` appears to work in markup, it’s because another class/rule (commonly `.border`) is providing a non-zero width.
